# CHERRY-PICK

## Git Cherry-Pick

- `git cherry-pick` lets me copy a specific commit from one branch onto another.

- Example:

    git cherry-pick abc1234

- This can be useful when I only want one particular change rather than an entire branch.

- It is more advanced and I probably will not need it regularly when starting out.

